From 3a363b4e9e75d29c45381901944421c83003916e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AEON-7 <aeon-7@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 00:41:48 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] [AEON R5-1] inkling2 ROCm: per-request residual-stream
 variant edits

Variants (AEON_VARIANT_DIR files and POST /aeon/variants) take optional
resid_dirs / resid_scales (same shapes as dirs / scales). After layer
application a, the mix entering application a+1 (the AEON_CAPTURE resid
tensor, all input streams, its own dtype) gets the per-row fp32 rank-K
removal y <- y - s r (r . y). Apps 17/29 edit the next pass's start input
(copy of prelude_dests); app 47 edits the final hidden state. o_proj-only,
residual-only or both, with separate scales/ranks; hot-added by rescan.

Same Triton kernel with an nrows argument (row r uses token r % nrows);
o_proj output is bitwise identical to before. Stock rows (vid 0) are never
touched; per-row math, so mixed batches equal single-variant launches.
