+
+Residual-stream edits (R5). A variant file may also carry
+    resid_dirs, resid_scales   same shapes as dirs / scales
+in which case, after layer application a, the stream entering application
+a + 1 (the tensor AEON_CAPTURE_WHAT=resid records, every input stream of it)
+gets the same per-row rank-K removal with resid_dirs[a] / resid_scales[a].
+For a = 47 that is the final hidden state fed to the LM head. For the last
+application of a loop pass (a = 17, 29) the edit goes to the next pass's
+start input (the pass restart discards the captured mix and re-reads the
+prelude's state). A variant may be o_proj-only (dirs/scales), residual-only
+(resid_dirs/resid_scales) or both; omitted keys mean no edit of that kind.
+Residual edits work in the stream's dtype (fp32 mixes in the loop, bf16
+elsewhere) with fp32 math. Stock rows stay untouched.
